    "result_text": "Sheet-wide claim numbers now restart each fiscal year, and all 4 acceptance tests pass under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**How numbering works now:** when a claim is opened and per-period numbering isn't in force, it gets `FY<yyyy>-<n>`. The fiscal year is worked out from the claim's due-by date, the same date that already places a claim in a period, using its own sheet's fiscal start month. Years are named by the calendar year their first day falls in, as elsewhere in the app. Each fiscal year counts from 1, and every sheet in a tree shares that year's sequence. Numbers already given are left as they are, and per-period numbering, when on, still takes precedence.\n\n**What changed (server only):**\n- `SheetService.nextClaimNumber(id, date)` now returns the formatted number. It locks the tree's sheets as before, reads the highest number already given for that year on any sheet in the tree, adds one, and stores the result on the claim's own sheet.\n- The per-year counters live in the existing `claim_sequence` table under the key `fy:<yyyy>`, so no schema migration was needed. Three supporting queries were added to `SheetRepository`.\n- `ClaimService.nextNumber` calls the new method. Open, split and reassign all go through it, so they all pick up the new format.\n- No front-end change was needed: the screen already shows the number as text.\n\nThe old single sheet-wide counter (`sheet.last_claim_number`) is no longer advanced. It and its repository methods are still there but unused.",
